Retry the PinWeaver tree reset when no credential is recorded on disk.

StateIsReady() decided whether to reset the PinWeaver merkle tree from the
existence of /home/.shadow/low_entropy_creds alone, but SignInHashTree's
constructor creates that directory before the reset is attempted. A failed
reset therefore leaves the directory behind with the TPM-side tree still
uninitialized, and every later call skips the reset forever -- so every
InsertCredential() fails with PW_ERR_TREE_INVALID and OOBE cannot persist a
PIN or a password. Triggered by an interrupted first boot (power cut/crash).

Also logs which reset path was taken; the skipped reset previously left no
trace in the log at all.

FYDE-564

